Algorithms implemented from peer-reviewed literature with clean-room C11/SIMD
implementations:
- Ville (1939), Étude critique de la notion de collectif
- Howard, Ramdas, McAuliffe, Sekhon (2021), Time-uniform, nonparametric,
  nonasymptotic confidence sequences (Annals of Statistics)
- Waudby-Smith & Ramdas (2024), Estimating means of bounded random variables
  by betting (JRSS-B)
- Vovk & Wang (2021), E-values: Calibration, combination and applications (AoS)
- Gibbs & Candès (2021, 2024), Adaptive Conformal Inference (NeurIPS / JMLR)
- Zaffran et al. (2022), Adaptive Conformal Predictions for Time Series (ICML)
- Angelopoulos, Candès, Tibshirani (2023), Conformal PID Control (NeurIPS)
- Wintenberger (2017), Optimal learning with Bernstein Online Aggregation (MLJ)
- Cohen, Duffield, Kaplan, Lund, Thorup (2011), Stream Sampling for Variance-
  Optimal Estimation of Subset Sums (SIAM J. Comput.)
- Cohen, Musco, Pachocki (2016), Online Row Sampling (APPROX/RANDOM)
- Boehm (2012), Can Seqlocks Get Along with Programming Language Memory Models?
